 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you doing? That's tough. Is he able to use a wheelchair or walker? Then keep trips as short as possible. Start at the front door, walk to the corner, the shop, and back again. Don't go up or down any stairs. If the landings are shallow, and he' stable on a chair, it's worth trying. Ask the building manager first. Take him in the car if it' shorter and easier. Park as close to the entrance as you can, and meet him outside. Some people will have already carried in bags. Keep an eye on his energy too. A few flights of stairs can drain someone's day. Is there anything else worrying him?",
